    "meaning": "Fixed residual-degree, candidate-order, edge-list, and output-word buffers for at most eight vertices."
  },
  "algorithm_details": {
    "primary": "Repeatedly select the highest positive residual degree (smallest vertex ID on ties), order all remaining vertices by residual degree descending then ID ascending, connect the selected vertex to the first d entries, and decrement those entries; reject a zero neighbor residual.",
    "independent_oracle": "Check graphicality with the Erdős-Gallai inequalities, then replay the same deterministic reduction using a priority queue keyed by negative residual degree and vertex ID; separately validate any realization certificate by simplicity and exact degree counts.",
    "complexity": "O(N^2 log N) bounded primary time and O(N^2) certificate space; N is at most eight."
  },
